              "en": "Tekken asks music to perform a different job from racing. Fighting is built from short pauses, readable impacts and characters who need to feel distinct before the player has mastered their move sets. Sano appears among the composers associated with the series' early period and brings an electronic practice already trained by arcade production. Here rhythm must sustain tension without covering the weight of hits, while synthesizers and samples help build a technological, aggressive world. The lesson is less obvious than a memorable melodic theme but just as important: a soundtrack can define the material texture of a game. In Tekken, sound suggests metal, energy, urban space and spectacle, helping every arena feel like an environment with its own temperature.",
