              "en": "Commander Keen also shows that the way a game is sold can become part of its design strategy. Apogee founder Scott Miller proposes distributing the first episode online as shareware and earning revenue from later episodes. Before the World Wide Web, the free file circulates through bulletin boards, copies among friends and software collections, turning each player into a possible distribution point. For a small team, that means reaching an audience and earning money without depending immediately on retail shelves. id preserves this logic of direct access with Wolfenstein 3D and Doom. The model does not eliminate publishers or stores, but it changes the order of events: players first try a substantial piece, then decide whether to fund the rest. Technology, design and distribution begin to move together.",
