              "en": "With Quake, id Software confronts a more radical problem: not simulating depth, but building a world in which geometry, characters and movement inhabit the same three-dimensional space. The new engine changes how levels, lighting and enemies are designed, while making free looking and aiming feel natural. Network and Internet multiplayer also turn that world into a shared place, encouraging clans, competition and a culture that will grow into esports. The cost is a difficult development process, later discussed by Romero in the game's postmortem. Quake therefore reveals the price of innovation: a technology can open a new language while putting enormous pressure on the group building it. After Doom, the engine is no longer merely a means of production; it becomes the field of research itself.",
